---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import EnquiryForm from '../components/EnquiryForm';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How More Than Mildly handles your information, preferences, enquiries, and privacy requests."
  ><div class="container legal-page">
    <span class="eyebrow">YOUR PRIVACY</span><h1>A little clarity.</h1><p
      class="legal-date"
    >
      Privacy policy · Last updated 6 September 2026
    </p><div class="prose">
      <p>
        This notice describes how More Than Mildly handles information through
        this publication. Use the form below to contact the team about privacy
        or your personal information.
      </p><h2>Information you give us</h2><p>
        If you send an enquiry, we store your name, email address, optional
        company name, and message so the team can respond. Please do not include
        sensitive personal information. Administrators have authenticated
        accounts managed through Netlify Identity.
      </p><h2>Information used to operate the site</h2><p>
        Likes use a signed browser identifier. We store a hash of that
        identifier with the article you liked. The total helps order articles,
        and is not displayed publicly. Notification subscriptions contain a
        browser push endpoint, encryption keys, and your time zone, allowing us
        to deliver the notifications you request.
      </p><p>
        The hosting provider processes technical information, including network
        addresses, for delivery and security. Our request limits use a
        short-lived hash to limit abuse. The application does not put your name,
        email, or search terms into analytics events.
      </p><h2>Optional measurement</h2><p>
        If you accept analytics and the integration is configured, Google
        Analytics can receive reading and interaction events. Meta and TikTok
        integrations remain disabled unless the publication enables them and you
        separately consent. We respect Global Privacy Control for advertising
        tracking. Read our <a href="/cookies">cookie policy</a> to manage choices.
      </p><h2>Why information is used</h2><p>
        We use information to deliver requested features, answer enquiries,
        maintain security, and, with consent, measure use of the publication.
        Depending on the applicable law and activity, processing may rely on
        consent, steps requested before a contract, or legitimate interests in
        operating and securing the service.
      </p><h2>Service providers and international processing</h2><p>
        Netlify provides hosting, database, image storage, and admin
        authentication. Browser push services deliver notifications. When
        enabled with consent, Google, Meta, and TikTok provide measurement
        services. These providers may process information in countries other
        than yours. Provider agreements and any required transfer safeguards
        must be considered for the services in use.
      </p><h2>Retention</h2><p>
        Notification delivery records are retained for up to 30 days.
        Notification subscriptions are removed when you unsubscribe or the push
        service reports an expired subscription. Enquiries stay available to the
        team until deleted. Like records remain until removed by the reader,
        removed through a privacy request, or the article is deleted. Hosting
        and measurement providers maintain their own configured retention
        periods.
      </p><h2>Your choices and rights</h2><p>
        Depending on your location, you may have rights to access, correct,
        delete, or receive a copy of personal information; object to or restrict
        certain uses; withdraw consent; or complain to a relevant privacy
        authority. California residents may also have rights to opt out of
        selling or sharing personal information and to exercise applicable
        rights without discrimination.
      </p><p>
        You can withdraw cookie consent in the footer, turn notifications off
        using the bell in the header, and submit a privacy request below. The
        team may need limited information to verify a request for personal data,
        but you do not need an account to opt out of advertising tracking.
      </p><h2>Children and young people</h2><p>
        This publication is available to a broad audience. We do not ask readers
        to provide a date of birth. Advertising pixels are disabled by default.
        If you believe a child has sent personal information that should be
        removed, contact us below.
      </p>
    </div><section id="request" class="privacy-request">
      <h2>Contact the privacy team</h2><p>
        Ask a question or request access, correction, or deletion of personal
        information.
      </p><EnquiryForm client:load kind="privacy" />
    </section>
  </div></Layout
>
